  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of bulk, mass, size and scale would be present a narrow, detached dwellinghouse at odds with the prominent built form in the area and harmful to the character of the streetscene.&nbsp; As such, the proposal is considered to be unacceptable and contrary to:Paragraphs 131 and 135&nbsp;of the National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF)&nbsp;(DLUHC, December 2023)Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy CP3&nbsp;Local Development Framework (LDF) Core Strategy (July 2010)Policy BP11&nbsp;of the&nbsp;Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011)Policies SP2 and DMD1&nbsp;of the&nbsp;Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19 Main Modifications version, February 2024)",
    "The bulk, mass, scale, siting and design of the proposed development would result in a loss of privacy, outlook, daylight, cause overshadowing and create an overbearing environment for neighbouring properties, especially flats 1A-D West Park Close. As such, the proposed development is deemed to be unacceptable and contrary to:The National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, December 2023)Policies GG1 and GG3 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy BP8 of the&nbsp;Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011)Policies DMD1 and DMS13 of the&nbsp;Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19 Main Modifications version, February 2024)"
  ],
